Resolved: The 429 responses were tied to push events. The only webhook subscribed to the `push` event was webhook_001 (https://hooks.novatech.dev/github/push, created 2024-10-05). I have removed that webhook, so push notifications to that endpoint should stop and the burst traffic from rapid successive pushes should no longer occur.

The Slack integration (webhook_003) subscribes only to `pull_request` and `issues`, so it was not the source of the push-related 429s. The deployments webhook (webhook_002) is also unchanged.

@carlos-mendez @erik-hoffman: please confirm on your side that the 429s have stopped during your next push sequence.
